/-!
# The rooms of the orthogonal addition gadgets

Generated by a program; do not edit.

In a slot of kind `addLe` / `addGe` (origin `g`), the three nook segments lie on the line
`x = g + 30`.  For every opening bounding the view of a designated guard, the part of the zone of
the slot template reachable from the nook without crossing the vertical door through that
opening is a room of `polyO` with that door (`…_room`, by `tmplRoomV`), contained in an explicit
box (`…_bounds`).  The nook segments (minus the pieces taken by the chain helpers) are edges of
the template (`…_bd`), and the open boxes left of them contain no point of the region, so no
point left of `x = g + 30` sees an interior point of a nook segment (`…_wall`).
-/

